s, not salary or job guarantees.", "profile": {"description": "Operates and checks water-treatment equipment and records what the process shows. Future role: Water Treatment Plant Operator; professional plant operation needs specific training and supervision.", "observable_behaviours": "Observe the Prepared Water Settle: compare the initial cloudy jar and the settled layers without shaking the jar. Record the liquid and sediment observations at the named times; Transfer and Filter: decant from Jar A into Jar B without disturbing settled soil; pass the liquid through filter paper into Cup C; keep vessel IDs attached to readings; Inspect What Paper Filtration Retains: distinguish source solutions, observe what the paper retains, and document the filtrate without merging their samples", "role_work_context": "A water-treatment facility monitors equipment, keeps operational readings and transfers reliable results for supervisor review. Students examine a simplified classroom separation process, not an operating plant.", "typical_work_activities": "Observe the prepared jar settling without disturbing sediment; Trace Jar A to Jar B to Cup C while recording volume readings; Identify visible material retained on filter paper; Keep equipment observations and exception records for review", "role_output_evidence": "Settling observation sheet; Decanting and filtration transfer log; Filter-paper observation note; Equipment-reading and handover checklist; Learning modules: RMR-CAP-L01-M01 - Observe the Prepared Water Settle (Core, step 1), RMR-CAP-L01-M02 - Transfer and Filter (Important, step 2), RMR-CAP-L04-M02 - Inspect What Paper Filtration Retains (Important, step 3)", "primary_riasec": "R", "secondary_riasec": "C", "tertiary_riasec": "I", "riasec_reason": "Realistic work centres on treatment equipment; Conventional methods protect checklists and readings; Investigative thinking helps spot unexpected changes and refer them for review.", "degree_gate": "Preferred", "direct_degree_mapping": "Diploma in Chemical Engineering; Diploma in Civil Engineering; Diploma in Environmental Engineering; B.Sc. Chemistry", "riasec_code_string": "RCI", "aptitude_profile": {"verbal_reasoning": 58, "logical_reasoning": 78, "numerical_reasoning": 76, "data_interpretation": 77, "pattern_recognition": 76, "spatial_reasoning": 84}, "big_five_profile": {"openness": 3, "conscientiousness": 5, "extraversion": 3, "agreeableness": 4, "emotional_stability": 5}, "work_values_profile": {"impact": 4, "status": 3, "autonomy": 3, "security": 5, "financial": 4, "lifestyle": 3, "creativity": 2, "leadership": 3}, "aptitude_assessment": {"areas": ["Spatial Reasoning", "Logical Reasoning", "Data Interpretation"], "rationale": "Water Plant Operator uses spatial reasoning, logical reasoning, data interpretation to observe the prepared jar settling without disturbing sediment, trace jar a to jar b to cup c while recording volume readings, and interpret source-based records. These priorities are proposed role demands, not measured learner aptitude."}, "big5_assessment": {"traits": ["Conscientiousness", "Emotional Stability", "Agreeableness"], "rationale": "Water Plant Operator benefits from conscientiousness, emotional stability, agreeableness when performing trace jar a to jar b to cup c while recording volume readings and following through on equipment-reading and handover checklist. Traits guide supportive coaching, not exclusion."}, "work_values_assessment": {"values": ["Security", "Impact", "Financial Growth"], "rationale": "This pathway may reward security, impact, financial growth through the work of observe the prepared jar settling without disturbing sediment and producing a clear settling observation sheet. These are possible work priorities, not salary or job guarantees."}}, "embedding_text": "ROLE\nName: Water Plant Operator\n\nCAREER CONTEXT\nIndustry: Water & Environmental Services\nDomain: Water Infrastructure Operations\nRole Family: Water Treatment Plant Operator\n\nROLE SUMMARY\nOperates and checks water-treatment equipment and records what the process shows. Future role: Water Treatment Plant Operator; professional plant operation needs specific training and supervision.\n\nWORK CONTEXT\nA water-treatment facility monitors equipment, keeps operational readings and transfers reliable results for supervisor review. Students examine a simplified classroom separation process, not an operating plant.\n\nTYPICAL WORK ACTIVITIES\nObserve the prepared jar settling without disturbing sediment; Trace Jar A to Jar B to Cup C while recording volume readings; Identify visible material retained on filter paper; Keep equipment observations and exception records for review\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES & ACTIONS\nObserve the Prepared Water Settle: compare the initial cloudy jar and the settled layers without shaking the jar. Record the liquid and sediment observations at the named times; Transfer and Filter: decant from Jar A into Jar B without disturbing settled soil; pass the liquid through filter paper into Cup C; keep vessel IDs attached to readings; Inspect What Paper Filtration Retains: distinguish source solutions, observe what the paper retains, and document the filtrate without merging their samples\n\nDELIVERABLES & OUTPUTS\nSettling observation sheet; Decanting and filtration transfer log; Filter-paper observation note; Equipment-reading and handover checklist; Learning modules: RMR-CAP-L01-M01 - Observe the Prepared Water Settle (Core, step 1), RMR-CAP-L01-M02 - Transfer and Filter (Important, step 2), RMR-CAP-L04-M02 - Inspect What Paper Filtration Retains (Important, step 3)\n\nINTEREST AND WORK-STYLE ALIGNMENT\nRealistic work centres on treatment equipment; Conventional methods protect checklists and readings; Investigative thinking helps spot unexpected changes and refer them for review.\n\nAPTITUDE ALIGNMENT\nKey areas: Spatial Reasoning, Logical Reasoning, Data Interpretation\nReadiness: Water Plant Operator uses spatial reasoning, logical reasoning, data interpretation to observe the prepared jar settling without disturbing sediment, trace jar a to jar b to cup c while recording volume readings, and interpret source-based records. These priorities are proposed role demands, not measured learner aptitude.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL ALIGNMENT\nKey traits: Conscientiousness, Emotional Stability, Agreeableness\nWork style: Water Plant Operator benefits from conscientiousness, emotional stability, agreeableness when performing trace jar a to jar b to cup c while recording volume readings and following through on equipment-reading and handover checklist. Traits guide supportive coaching, not exclusion.\n\nWORK-VALUE ALIGNMENT\nKey values: Security, Impact, Financial Growth\nMotivation: This pathway may reward security, impact, financial growth through the work of observe the prepared jar settling without disturbing sediment and producing a clear settling observation sheet. These are possible work priorities, not salary or job guarantees.\n\nEDUCATION AND ELIGIBILITY\nGate: Preferred\nStreams: Diploma in Chemical Engineering; Diploma in Civil Engineering; Diploma in Environmental Engineering; B.Sc. Chemistry\n"}'::jsonb;
