934b8-fbe6-5fe9-aec6-81d9c4aa7878", "riasecCode": "CEI", "whyThisRole": "Numerical practice and organised teamwork can support school-level water budgets, project plans and responsible business proposals. Explores how people calculate costs, compare resource needs and check that water-project numbers are supported by records."}, {"name": "Water Business Planner", "occupationId": "41aa9177-f4c9-5ce5-a653-d1c27ab1b9f2", "riasecCode": "ECS", "whyThisRole": "Numerical practice and organised teamwork can support school-level water budgets, project plans and responsible business proposals. Explores how a team organises water-related tasks, compares costs and prepares a practical plan from available evidence."}], "exploreLater": [{"name": "River Protection Planner", "occupationId": "536f691c-f471-535b-af4c-5d46f2714f4c", "riasecCode": "SIE", "whyThisRole": "Interest in environmental impact and communication can develop through supervised river protection, community support and policy evidence activities. Explores how people plan river-protection actions after checking field observations and the limits of the available evidence."}, {"name": "Community Water Helper", "occupationId": "332bf8da-a837-563d-bfb8-ce1f6795a6f7", "riasecCode": "SEC", "whyThisRole": "Interest in environmental impact and communication can develop through supervised river protection, community support and policy evidence activities. Helps communities understand water observations, plan informed action and communicate uncertainty clearly. Future role: Community Water Programme Coordinator; this is school-level career exploration."}, {"name": "Water Policy Adviser", "occupationId": "e2325fb1-a705-5ba9-82aa-2f8368312a70", "riasecCode": "SEI", "whyThisRole": "Interest in environmental impact and communication can develop through supervised river protection, community support and policy evidence activities. Explores how water decisions can be explained to communities and authorities using documented evidence and its limitations."}]}}, "streamRecommendation": {"recommendedStream": "Science — PCMB", "displayName": "Science — PCMB", "stream": "Science — PCMB", "category": "science", "confidence": "High", "matchScore": 88, "reasoning": {"interests": "Investigative, practical and structured interests support scientific exploration.", "aptitude": "Keep developing numerical reasoning, data interpretation and scientific explanations.", "personality": "Curiosity and careful follow-through support laboratory learning and sustained study."}, "subjects": {"core": ["Physics", "Chemistry", "Mathematics", "Biology"], "additional": ["English", "Computer Science"]}, "careerPaths": ["Water Plant Designer", "Water Health Researcher", "Water Quality Tester", "Water Project Manager", "Water Budget Expert", "Water Business Planner", "River Protection Planner", "Community Water Helper", "Water Policy Adviser"], "entranceExams": [], "alternativeStream": {"stream": "Science — PCM", "reason": "Consider PCM if engineering and mathematical modelling become stronger interests than biological study."}, "preparationAdvice": "Strengthen Grade 10 science and mathematics; discuss workload, subject availability and interests with teachers.", "source": "user-requested development fixture; workbook role routing", "isGrade10": true}, "overallSummary": "You show curiosity about how things work, a careful approach to evidence and an interest in science and mathematics. Science — PCMB can help you explore water treatment, water-quality testing and health-related research while keeping several future study options open. Build confidence through supervised experiments, clear calculations and practical projects, and use teamwork to explore water planning and river protection. These interests can evolve as you learn; review your subject choices with your teachers and family.", "skillGap": {"currentStrengths": ["Scientific curiosity", "Careful observation", "Structured records", "Team communication"], "priorityA": [{"skill": "Transfer and Filter", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L01-M02", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can decant from Jar A into Jar B without disturbing settled soil; pass the liquid through filter paper into Cup C; keep vessel IDs attached to readings. Required evidence: Transfer-and-filtration evidence with the collected volume. Scientific boundary: Clearer appearance is not proof of drinking-water safety.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Calculate the Collected Volume", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L01-M03", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can match vessel and volume; subtract 200 - 175 = 25 mL; simplify 25/200 = 1/8; calculate 12.5% not collected and 87.5% collected. Required evidence: A labelled volume, fraction and percentage calculation record. Scientific boundary: The 25 mL difference is not the dry mass of mud removed.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Prepare the School-Tank Evidence Note", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L01-M04", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can use the supported volume and observation records; distinguish what separation shows from what drinking-water safety would require; prepare a short note. Required evidence: A school-tank evidence note with findings, limits and a next step. Scientific boundary: Do not claim that the school tank is safe to drink from.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Test the Three Coded Liquids", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L02-M01", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can keep cup IDs separate; compare each recorded strip before and after testing; enter the colour observation without assuming the category. Required evidence: A coded-sample litmus observation table. Scientific boundary: A colour observation should not be replaced by an invented result.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Investigate the Cup B Conflict", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L02-M02", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can retain T1 and T2; record a clean-tool fresh-strip T3 separately; compare all three and flag the unexplained T2 conditions. Required evidence: A Cup B discrepancy and controlled-retest log. Scientific boundary: Do not claim contamination or another cause unless proven.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Finish the Cost and Finding Log", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L02-M04", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can multiply number of strips by unit cost, subtract expenditure from the budget, and write what the test evidence supports. Required evidence: A verified cost calculation and scientific finding log. Scientific boundary: A low testing cost does not make incomplete findings conclusive.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Compare the Two Field Reports", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L03-M01", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can align source ID, conditions, observations and missing fields side by side; identify which differences can be compared fairly. Required evidence: A two-report comparison and list of missing controls. Scientific boundary: Different conditions must not be presented as a controlled experiment.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Calculate Runoff Across Three Trials", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L03-M03", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can calculate means 160 mL and 100 mL; compute 64% and 40% runoff; report the 24-percentage-point gap. Required evidence: A three-trial mean, percentage and comparison table. Scientific boundary: 24 percentage points is a runoff-share gap, not dry soil mass lost.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Write a Fair Field-Study Proposal", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L03-M04", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can specify the research question, matched variables, measurements and evidence needed; state where conclusions remain limited. Required evidence: A fair field-study proposal with evidence and next actions. Scientific boundary: Missing slope or rainfall controls must be made explicit.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Inspect What Paper Filtration Retains", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L04-M02", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can distinguish source solutions, observe what the paper retains, and document the filtrate without merging their samples. Required evidence: A two-sample filtration observation and scientific explanation. Scientific boundary: Visible filtration alone does not prove dissolved salt removal.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Evaluate the Filter Advertisement", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L04-M04", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can quote the claim, compare it with supported filtration results, identify missing controls and write a bounded decision. Required evidence: A claim-check decision with evidence and limitations. Scientific boundary: Do not claim that dissolved salt removal was verified.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Compare Teacher-Prepared Reference Liquids", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L05-M01", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can match each strip to its own sample, compare observed colours with the correct kit chart and record the classification. Required evidence: A sample-by-sample indicator evidence table. Scientific boundary: The reference chart must be supplied; pH or appearance alone is not safety proof.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Interpret the Fictional R-26 Report", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L05-M04", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can keep pH beside each sample ID; classify A near-neutral, B acidic and C basic; identify untested safety indicators. Required evidence: An R-26 report interpretation and missing-evidence log. Scientific boundary: These pH values do not certify water as safe to drink.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}, {"skill": "Prepare the Water-Authority Handover", "capabilityCode": "RMR-CAP-L05-M05", "currentLevel": 0, "targetLevel": 1, "whyNeeded": "Learner can summarise verified observations, missing measurements, limits and the responsible next testing or referral action. Required evidence: A water-authority handover note with evidence and unresolved questions. Scientific boundary: No water-use clearance without the necessary accredited safety testing.", "howToBuild": "Complete the source-based activity with teacher guidance."}], "priorityB": [{"skill": "Responsible scientific communication", "whyNeeded": "Avoid unsupported water-safety conclusions.", "howToBuild": "Separate observations, calculations, uncertainties and missing evidence."}], "recommendedTrack": "Water Science, Health and Engineering", "learningTracks": [{"track": "Water Science, Health and Engineering", "suggestedIf": "Curiosity about evidence, careful records and science-and-mathematics interests support exploring water treatment, testing and health-related questions.", "topics": "Water & Environmental Engineering, Water Quality & Laboratory Science"}, {"track": "Water Project, Budget and Business Planning", "suggestedIf": "Numerical practice and organised teamwork can support school-level water budgets, project plans and responsible business proposals.", "topics": "Water Operations & Planning, Water Project Pla